From: edde746 <86283021+edde746@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:10:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] videotoolbox: skip the wait after a synchronous decode

videotoolbox_session_decode_frame() called
VTDecompressionSessionWaitForAsynchronousFrames() after every frame. It
passes no decode flags, so the session decodes synchronously: the output
callback has run by the time VTDecompressionSessionDecodeFrame() returns,
and the wait finds nothing pending. The decoder runs in another process
on Apple platforms, so the wait was still a round trip to it for every
frame.

Ask the session for its info flags and wait only when it reports the
decode as asynchronous (kVTDecodeInfo_Asynchronous).

diff --git a/libavcodec/videotoolbox.c b/libavcodec/videotoolbox.c
index 2d2f7a2..d2c10f9 100644
--- a/libavcodec/videotoolbox.c
+++ b/libavcodec/videotoolbox.c
@@ -759,6 +759,7 @@ static void videotoolbox_decoder_callback(void *opaque,
 static OSStatus videotoolbox_session_decode_frame(AVCodecContext *avctx)
 {
     OSStatus status;
+    VTDecodeInfoFlags info_flags = 0;
     CMSampleBufferRef sample_buf;
     AVVideotoolboxContext *videotoolbox = videotoolbox_get_context(avctx);
     VTContext *vtctx = avctx->internal->hwaccel_priv_data;
@@ -774,8 +775,13 @@ static OSStatus videotoolbox_session_decode_frame(AVCodecContext *avctx)
                                                sample_buf,
                                                0,       // decodeFlags
                                                NULL,    // sourceFrameRefCon
-                                               0);      // infoFlagsOut
-    if (status == noErr)
+                                               &info_flags);
+    // With no decode flags the session decodes synchronously: the output
+    // callback has run by the time DecodeFrame returns, and the session
+    // leaves kVTDecodeInfo_Asynchronous clear to say so. Waiting after such
+    // a decode only costs a round trip to the decoder process, so wait only
+    // when the session reports the decode as asynchronous.
+    if (status == noErr && (info_flags & kVTDecodeInfo_Asynchronous))
         status = VTDecompressionSessionWaitForAsynchronousFrames(videotoolbox->session);
 
     CFRelease(sample_buf);
